      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I could reproduce the issue.\n\nThe issue title should be like, \"Canvas UI of some worlds doesn't respond to mouse clicks in desktop mode.\" (The title is written in Japanese, and Canny seems to fail to generate the URL correctly.)\n\nI took a video. I record click sounds of my IRL mouse to clarify when I operate it.\n\n- 0:00 The screen size is 1920 x 1200. This video captures the whole screen.\n\n- 0:04 Tested with build 1664\n\n- 0:09 Tested with the world \"Avatar Dance Stage\" noted on the post. There are two radio buttons to select the music.\n\n- 0:12 No problem when the window is maximised. \n\n- 0:25 I changed the window size to middle-sized (about 3/4 of the screen)\n\n- 0:26 The upper button doesn't respond to the clicks\n\n- 0:31 Trying the free cursor by pressing the TAB key\n\n- 0:35 It works\n\n- 0:36 But sometimes it doesn't (depending on the position?)\n\n- 0:55 The lay cast to the Canvas seems fine, maybe. (The blue mouse cursor disappears/appears on the edge of the UI region)\n\n- 1:17 The mouse operations on the Main Menu work fine with this medium-sized window.\n\n- 1:30 Trying small-sized window (about 1/2  of the screen)\n\n- 1:33 It works. (I have no idea what's going on.)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
